# The day's routines as lines (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The bitten, the clock and what you carry"): shift
# change at 05:30 and 17:30, supper at 18:30, the night watch at 20:30. No clocks of their own: the
# game hour opens and closes them. And the epilogue week, said in passing.

conv bark.named.bastion.shiftchange
for named:bastion, post:bastion
when hour>=17 & hour<18
bark
voice bastion

node start
  say? hour>=17 & hour<18 :: "Shift change. Two minutes. Don't stand in the doorway."
  say "Shift change. Two minutes."

conv bark.occupant.supper
for occupant
when hour>=18 & hour<19 & !house:died
bark
voice haven

node start
  say? house:short :: "Supper's thin. Sit anyway. It's grace first, then argue about the potatoes."
  say "Sit, it's grace. You can eat standing up afterwards, like the rest of us."

conv bark.named.bastion.watch
for named:bastion, post:bastion
when hour>=20 & hour<22
bark
voice bastion

node start
  say "Night watch. Lights down. If you're staying, you're on the roll."

conv bark.occupant.epilogue
for occupant
when epilogue
bark
voice haven

node start
  say? cure_held:everyone :: "Somebody brought it to the door. Didn't stop for soup. Who doesn't stop for soup?"
  say? cure_held:bastion :: "We're on the list. Everyone's on a list. It's almost restful."
  say "Processing at the checkpoints, the loudspeakers say. Nobody's gone up yet."

conv bark.named.redhand.epilogue
for named:redhand
when epilogue
bark
voice redhand

node start
  say? cure_held:redhand :: "Prices on the board, cure in the crate. Best week we've ever had."
  say "Cure's out. Toll's still a tin. Some things are sacred."

conv bark.named.halcyon.epilogue
for named:halcyon
when epilogue
bark
voice halcyon

node start
  say "Results are in. The writing-up takes longer than the work did."
